harnessloop/plugins/harnessloop/skills/harnessloop-setup/SKILL.md:82:## S3 Cost And Context Policy → `setup/cost-context-policy.md`
harnessloop/plugins/harnessloop/skills/harnessloop-setup/SKILL.md:86:Write each field at its exact heading-path location, not by label alone. Several labels repeat across the template: `Core decisions` appears under Main Session, Codex, and Claude Code (3 independent slots); `Low-context execution` and `Adversarial review` each appear under Delegation Rules, Codex, and Claude Code (3 slots each); `Independent investigation` appears under Codex and Claude Code (2 slots). `Main Session > Responsibilities > Core decisions`, `Model Policy > Codex > Core decisions`, and `Model Policy > Claude Code > Core decisions` take different source content (main-session orchestration duties vs. each model's decision-making boundary) — never write one sentence into all three and call it done.
harnessloop/plugins/harnessloop/skills/harnessloop-setup/SKILL.md:88:Do not touch `Execution Delegation Matrix`: its 8 `Decision` rows are already protocol-level prefilled content (from the loop skill's own delegation matrix), not a question for this step.
