     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""Settle per-round token cost from Claude Code session transcripts.
     3	
     4	Reads the project's transcript files (JSONL under
     5	~/.claude/projects/<escaped-project-path>/), aggregates API usage recorded on
     6	assistant turns since the last settlement marker, and prints a markdown
     7	`## Cost` section ready to paste into the round's round-summary.md.
     8	
     9	The computation is fully local and deterministic — transcripts must never be
    10	read into the model context; only this script's short summary is.
    11	
    12	Attribution heuristic: an assistant turn whose message content mentions
    13	`.harnessloop` is counted as protocol-attributed. This is a heuristic, not an
    14	exact split; the output labels it as such.
    15	
    16	Cost estimation is optional: create `.harnessloop/local/cost-prices.json`
    17	with USD-per-million-token rates, e.g.
    18	    {"input": 3.0, "cache_write": 3.75, "cache_read": 0.3, "output": 15.0}
    19	No model prices are baked into this script.
    20	
    21	The settlement marker (`.harnessloop/local/cost-marker.json`) stores how many
    22	transcript lines were already counted, so each run reports only the window
    23	since the previous run. Multi-session rounds are covered: all transcript
    24	files for the project are tracked independently.
    25	
    26	Message-id dedup: Claude Code writes one JSONL line per content block of an
    27	assistant message (thinking/tool_use/text/...), and every line for the same
    28	`message.id` repeats that message's full usage snapshot. Lines are grouped by
    29	`message.id` and each id's usage is counted exactly once (see `settle()` for
    30	the dedup and cross-settlement-window contract, including how the marker
    31	carries forward a message that is still being written when this script runs
    32	mid-turn).
    33	
    34	Exit codes: 0 = settled, 2 = transcript directory not found or usage error.
    35	"""
