   163	    partial-or-full group next run.
   164	
   165	    To prevent that, a message's usage is added to `totals` only once its
   166	    group is known to be *closed* — i.e. once a line with a different
   167	    (or absent) message.id is observed after it. The still-open group at
   168	    end-of-file is carried forward in the returned offsets as
   169	    `pending_id` / `pending_usage` / `pending_attributed` instead of being
   170	    billed; the next run resumes merging into it before deciding whether to
   171	    close and bill it. Net effect: every message.id is billed exactly once,
   172	    by whichever run first sees a line for a different subsequent id. The
   173	    trade-off is that the very last open message in a transcript (e.g. the
   174	    one invoking this script) has its usage deferred to the next
   175	    settlement rather than counted immediately — under-counting a handful
   176	    of tokens at the tail is preferable to the multi-x over-counting this
   177	    replaces. Lines without a message.id cannot be correlated at all and are
