     9	## Artifact Health Values
    10	
    11	- `valid`: evidence exists, is fresh enough, and can be cited.
    12	- `stale`: evidence exists but violates freshness or drift rules.
    13	- `missing`: evidence path or source is absent.
    14	- `inconclusive`: evidence exists but cannot support acceptance.
    15	- `blocked`: evidence requires human access or external setup.
    16	
    17	## Claim Support Values
    18	
    19	- `supports`: supports the claim being tested.
    20	- `refutes`: refutes the claim being tested.
    21	- `partial`: supports only part of the claim.
    22	- `unrelated`: valid artifact but not relevant to the claim.
    23	- `unknown`: claim relationship has not been assessed.
    24	
    25	## Acceptance Effect Values
    26	
    27	- `pass`: contributes to accepting a round.
    28	- `fail`: contributes to rejecting a round.
    29	- `neutral`: cited but not decisive.
    30	- `blocked`: cannot be evaluated without access or human action.
    31	
    32	## Evidence Types
    33	
    34	- static
    35	- dynamic
    36	- runtime
    37	- source
    38	- human-confirmation
